    {
      "id": "lima-vz-versioned",
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lima-vm/lima/v2.1.4/website/content/en/docs/config/vmtype/vz.md",
      "accessed_at": "2026-09-07T03:27:10.808278+00:00",
      "applicability": "Lima v2.1.4 tag matches installed CLI.",
      "http_status": 200,
      "body_sha256": "8b9692965d47c3bf6caaace5628ef7ab8e9cb0a22211f756d198e7c35b4fda3e",
      "excerpts": [
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "weight: 2"
        },
        {
          "line": 4,
          "text": "---"
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "| \u26a1 Requirement | Lima >= 0.14, macOS >= 13.0 |"
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "|-------------------|-----------------------------|"
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "\"vz\" option makes use of native virtualization support provided by macOS Virtualization.Framework."
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": "\"vz\" has been the default driver for macOS hosts since Lima v1.0."
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": "An example configuration (no need to be specified manually):"
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "{{< tabpane text=true >}}"
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": "{{% tab header=\"CLI\" %}}"
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "```bash"
        },
        {
          "line": 17,
          "text": "limactl start --vm-type=vz"
        },
        {
          "line": 28,
          "text": "{{% /tab %}}"
        },
        {
          "line": 29,
          "text": "{{< /tabpane >}}"
        },
        {
          "line": 30,
          "text": "### Caveats"
        },
        {
          "line": 31,
          "text": "- \"vz\" option is only supported on macOS 13 or above"
        },
        {
          "line": 32,
          "text": "- Virtualization.framework doesn't support running \"intel guest on arm\" and vice versa"
        },
        {
          "line": 33,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 34,
          "text": "### Known Issues"
        },
        {
          "line": 35,
          "text": "- \"vz\" doesn't support `legacyBIOS: true` option, so guest machine like `centos-stream` and `oraclelinux-8` will not work on Intel Mac."
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": "- When running lima using \"vz\", `${LIMA_HOME}/<INSTANCE>/serial.log` will not contain kernel boot logs"
        },
        {
          "line": 37,
          "text": "- On Intel Mac with macOS prior to 13.5, Linux kernel v6.2 (used by Ubuntu 23.04, Fedora 38, etc.) is known to be unbootable on vz."
        },
        {
          "line": 38,
          "text": "  kernel v6.3 and later should boot, as long as it is booted via GRUB."
        },
        {
          "line": 39,
          "text": "  https://github.com/lima-vm/lima/issues/1577#issuecomment-1565625668"
        },
        {
          "line": 40,
          "text": "  The issue is fixed in macOS 13.5."
        }
      ]
    },
